    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0421" n="305" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg305"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.304 M28/58.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 21037.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-02-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 10, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Under date of December 6, 1910, President
                    Gómez requested in a letter addressed to the President<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d427-f1"/> that a part of the battleship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Maine</hi> be delivered to the Republic of Cuba for memorial purposes.
                    Subsequently the Secretary of Public Works of Cuba addressed a letter to the
                    engineer office in charge, asking that the after-turret of the vessel intact,
                    with its guns and their mounts, be furnished for such purpose.</p>
                <p>Under authority of the Act of Congress approved December 22, 1911,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d427-f2"/> I have this day approved the transfer of the said
                    after-turret intact, with guns and their mounts and some of the shells belonging
                    to same, to the Republic of Cuba for the purpose above indicated, and have the
                    honor to request that the Department of State will so inform the President of
                    the Republic of Cuba.</p>
                <p>A copy of the President’s letter to President Gómez on the subject is also
                    transmitted herewith.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d427-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">H. L. Stimson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
